From: Greg Gage <zedle@zedle.com>
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: alienware-wmi-wmax: Add G-Mode, power, thermal and
 platform information

Some AWCC models list the G-Mode thermal profile (0xAB) in
Thermal_Information but have no GameShiftStatus method (0x25). The
Alienware x17 R2 is one: its WMAX returns 0xFFFFFFFF for 0x25, so with
force_gmode=1 every platform profile change fails with -EBADRQC.

On such models G-Mode is a thermal profile like any other and is
activated with Thermal_Control. This patch:

- Adds a "gmode" attribute on the WMAX WMI device, visible when 0xAB is
  listed and G-Mode is not already handled through GameShiftStatus.
  Writing 1 activates 0xAB and remembers the current profile; writing 0
  restores it (or the BIOS default profile, Thermal_Information 0x0A).
  Selecting a platform profile while G-Mode is on simply replaces it.
  Platform profile listeners are notified on every change.

- Checks GameShiftStatus once at probe when the gmode quirk or
  force_gmode asks for it. If the BIOS rejects it, warn once and keep
  the regular performance profile instead of failing every profile
  change.

- Adds read-only "default_profile" (Thermal_Information 0x0A) and
  "cooling_type" (Thermal_Information 0x01) attributes.

- Adds a read-only "power_info" group from PowerInformation (0x1C):
  "adapter_count" (op 1), "adapter_watts" (op 2, one value per present
  adapter) and "adapter_status" (op 4: ok, undersized, unsupported, or
  the raw value).

Each attribute is only created when its WMI call succeeds at probe.

The MODULE_VERSION hunk in alienware-wmi-base.c marks the out-of-tree
(DKMS) build and is not meant for upstream.
---

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/dell/alienware-wmi-base.c b/drivers/platform/x86/dell/alienware-wmi-base.c
